{"availability":"available","full":"Lyellr88/marm-memory","name":"marm-memory","description":"Local-first 3-in-1 AI memory layer & MCP server for Claude Code, Codex, Grok, Gemini, VS Code and Cursor. Fuses session history, codebase indexing & concept graphs in SQLite. Enables zero-cloud, privacy-first context & instant recall, supports multi-agent swarms.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":418,"forks":90,"created":"2025-06-10T06:36:49Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:17:41Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"MARM-main","homepage":"https://lyellr88.github.io/marm-memory","topics":["agent-memory","ai-agents","ai-memory","claude-code","codex-cli","developer-tools","embeddings","indexing-engine","knowledge-graph","llm","local-first","long-term-memory","mcp","mcp-servers","model-context-protocol","persistent-memory","rag","self-hosted","sematic-search","sqlite"],"demo":"https://lyellr88.github.io/marm-memory","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.804Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.804Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.804Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.804Z","stars":418,"forks":90}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Contributions welcome! Browse open issues to contribute, or join the MARM Discord to share workflows, get setup help, and connect with other builders.","Your AI forgets everything. MARM Memory doesn't.","marm-memory gives your agents a private, shared memory for the context that normally gets lost between chats: decisions, research, fixes, notes, and project history. Switch from Claude Code to Codex or Gemini without losing the context already gathered."],"features":["🧠 Core Memory (8 tools) stores conversations, notes, notebook entries, and summaries so they stay searchable.","💻 Code Graph (6 tools) maps your repository so agents can find symbols, follow code paths, and understand the project without rereading it all. Point it at a repo once and it keeps itself current as you work.","🧩 Concept Graph (2 tools) connects people, decisions, errors, and ideas from your stored memories, with links back to relevant code when available. It builds itself as you store memories."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md","fingerprint":"d66c496927c8af2e9de38233dbb4c0918cf90ffa03dc40fa452b3f9e91c2cab3","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.918Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.918Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Contributions welcome! Browse open issues to contribute, or join the MARM Discord to share workflows, get setup help, and connect with other builders.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"> Docker HTTP requires an API key because it exposes MARM as a network server; STDIO stays local to the client process and does not need one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The other checks: the operator's auto-apply switch is on; the proposal is re-resolved when the decision is made and is still new; one line of 12 to 300 characters; nothing that looks like a credential, whether labelled (apikey=) or in a known token format (provider keys, a bearer value, a JWT, a URL carrying a password). reviewmode=\"guardrails\" on marmdistill makes the same…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"d66c496927c8af2e9de38233dbb4c0918cf90ffa03dc40fa452b3f9e91c2cab3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.920Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T07:17:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Lyellr88/marm-memory/blob/MARM-main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:04.928Z","hash":"d66c49